WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you?
-I'm well.

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am so happy
to see you, always.

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
we already talked about

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.840
our Michael Cohen stuff tonight.
-Whew.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.707 line:92%
-So we got that out of the way.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:11.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know, people
don't realize there's a cost.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.445 line:92%
There's a cost for everyone.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that everybody
who was on television

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
this morning
had to pay that cost --

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.784 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
you particularly.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:19.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were
on "Kelly" this morning.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:20.020 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this happened while you
were getting interviewed.

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She thought
for years and years and years

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:28.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
and found herself
kind of on autopilot, and --

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:31.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Special report.
Michael Cohen testifies.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you very much.
-How dare they!

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm ready to zip it
at any moment.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They should let you now
go on Congress

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.473
and say what you were gonna say.
Yeah.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:44.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, God. I get agita
just, like, thinking of that.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:47.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But this is a wonderful show,
in its second season now.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.315 line:92%
Three moms who commit a crime

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then
the repercussions of that.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:53.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you enjoy --
Do moms come up to you now

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
and say that that
looks like an interesting way

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go about things?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:59.893 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Moms, women, yes.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
People find the show
very empowering.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:05.598
It's sisters, best friends
having each other's back

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.268 size:84% position:42% line:92%
no matter what happens.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.135 line:92%
So people are like, "I just --

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.671
I love how they're taking things
into their own hands."

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.173 line:92%
And I'm like, "Well, I mean,

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:15.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're doing
really stupid stuff."

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:16.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, like,
you know, within reason.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you think having done it
for a couple years --

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:23.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you think
you'd be at crime?

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.819
-I think --
I think I would be a little bit

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:28.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
smarter than my character.
-Oh, that's nice.

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:29.289 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's good, yeah.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But then --
But maybe not --

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:33.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, when I had to make
a quick decision,

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.094 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I might make mistakes.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think I would cover
my tracks a little bit better.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right, that's good.
-Yeah.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you have
two incredible co-stars,

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
both of whom have been here --
Retta and Mae Whitman.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they talk a lot.
I hope it's true.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:45.705
They say that you were very
close, the three of you.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.540 size:75% position:38%
-You hope it's true.
-Well, I would hate

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.910
if you said now like,
"No, the minute they say 'cut,'

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.045 line:92%
we go our separate ways."

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:54.447 size:88% position:44%
-No, we've been texting
each other all day long.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:59.319
They are two of my best friends
and amazing actresses.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.320 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I couldn't be luckier.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, we text each other
till like 2:00 in the morning.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:06.693
Retta will finally be like,
"I have to go to bed. Stop."

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:10.497
And we're all sending selfies
of ourselves laying in bed.

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:11.898 line:92%
-Your mom was not a criminal,

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you had
a very interesting mom.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.201 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:16.636 line:92%
Your mom was a hypnotherapist.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, she was not a criminal.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:21.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I can imagine,
as a kid, like,

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
having a mom
as a hypnotherapist,

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.177 line:92%
was that a cool -- did you --

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:26.913
could you appreciate that
that was cooler than most moms?

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.516 size:84% position:42%
-It was. It was sort of
a neighborhood trick.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:34.454 size:88% position:44%
She would practice on us
when she was learning,

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:36.756
and so we would have
the neighborhood kids come over,

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:37.490 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and we would be like --

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.460
you know, go through the process
of putting them in hypnosis,

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.427 line:92%
and then we would be like,

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You're gonna forget
the number 5,"

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they'd be like,
"Okay, wake up.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:46.399 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Now count your fingers."

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:49.602 size:84% position:42%
"One, two, three, four,
six, seven -- no way!"

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "No way!"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:52.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No way.
Wait, one, two."

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we'd be like, "Ha ha!
We did it!"

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.676
-I mean, that would be the
coolest thing in the world.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:59.279
-It was cool.
I'm sure we were all faking it,

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, you know...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seemed cool.
-Last time you were here,

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:06.586
we talked about "Mad Men"
and the end of that show.

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:09.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
You -- I still
can't believe this story.

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:10.890 line:92%
Your agent did not want you

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
to take the part
of Joel -- uh, Joan.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:14.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
Or Joel.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Or Joel.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:18.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
Said, "I think both of these
are bad for you."

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:18.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:21.501
-Yeah. I mean, at the time,
AMC didn't have any programing.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-And it was a period piece,

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:28.074
and they just didn't think
I was gonna make them any money.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:30.009 line:92%
And they just -- they weren't --

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:32.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
I decided, I said, "I love it.
I really --

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just feel really, really
strongly about it."

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were like,
"That's so great.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:37.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
No one wants
to work with you here."

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow! So you fully got let go
by your agency?

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I did.
-Wow. That's amazing.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.357
-Yeah.
-But also kind of great, right?

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:47.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause then you didn't have
to give them commission on it.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's true.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:52.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But this is -- this, to me,
is such a cool story.

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:55.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys had to --
There was a long delay

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.804
between when you shot the pilot
and when you started the show.

00:03:57.804 --> 00:04:00.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so you knew you had a job,
which is a thing --

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
not a lot of actors
live in that moment

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:04.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they're about
to start a job.

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so you then took on
another job

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:08.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was not
an acting job at all.

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:11.784
-We had this about a year
where we were being held,

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Matt Weiner,
the creator of the show,

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:14.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
was still working on
"The Sopranos,"

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:17.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so we couldn't work
on anything else

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:19.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause we were
in this holding pattern,

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:21.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I had always wanted
to be a florist.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-So I went to a local florist

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I really admired,
and I said,

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Would you ever
take on an intern

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:31.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I could learn
from your designers?"

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they kind of looked at me
like I was crazy.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were like,
"Well, I mean, we could use

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
some extra help
at Mother's Day."

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.212
And I was like, "Okay.
Well, I'll just do that."

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:41.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they hired me
for a short amount of time,

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:44.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I did a couple holidays
in the meantime.

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:45.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you ever have friends
who came in

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:48.488 size:88% position:44%
and saw you as a florist
and were like, "Oh, no."

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:49.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:52.158
No, quite -- quite often,
they would be coming in

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.593 line:92%
to buy flowers for their wives,

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:56.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I remember my friend
Craig Bierko came in,

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:58.431 line:92%
and he went -- "Oh -- hey."

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:01.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Like, "Oh."

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"No, it's -- it's okay.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:04.637 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I think I have a job.

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:05.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just have always
wanted to do this."

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:09.242
And now he's like, "That was
so badass when you did that."

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:09.909 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:12.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like a badass florist.
-Yeah.

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:13.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's true,
because I think, like,

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
as an actor like, you never --
you'll like --

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:17.050
You get a chance to, like,
pretend to be a florist,

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
but to actually
get to be a florist

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:19.585 line:92%
is probably a lot cooler.

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:21.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I thought
I was pretty good at it, too.

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:23.723
I was taking orders, getting --
you know, sending things out.

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:24.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was kind of like --
I was --

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:26.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I would imagine
high-pressure because --

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:29.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I do, because, I mean,
if a guy is calling

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:30.163 line:92%
to get flowers for his wife,

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:31.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
you don't want to blow that
for him.

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:33.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like he's already
in trouble, probably.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:35.902
-People come in for, like,
either really sad reasons,

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:37.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
bad reasons,
or really happy reasons.

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:39.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-There's not an in between.

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:41.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No one's like, "It's Tuesday.
I'm gonna go get flowers."

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:44.210
-Yeah. You're sort of like,
"Ooh-ooh. What'd you do?"

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.411 line:92%
Like, "How big should this be?"

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:46.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "How many
do we want to get here?"

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:50.883
-And then, I want to ask about
this because I'm assuming that,

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:52.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
you've done a lot of things,

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:53.886 line:92%
but "Mad Men" must be a show

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:55.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
people ask you about
all the time.

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:58.958 size:88% position:44%
And does it get tiring
hearing about it or not?

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:02.028 size:78% position:39%
-No, it's fantastic.
You know, it's funny.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:03.996 line:92%
People are very sweet about it,

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:07.100
and they'll come up and be like,
"You must hate this,

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:10.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
but your show, like,
changed my life."

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:12.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
And like, "Your character
was so inspiring."

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.173 line:92%
I'm like, "Yeah, I hate that."

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
Like, that's terrible.

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:17.543 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It's so nice to hear.

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:18.911 line:92%
And the way people watch TV now,

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:20.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
people are sometimes
just discovering it now.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:21.514 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Of course.

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:23.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And people
are still binge-watching it

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:24.283 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
or rewatching it.

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:25.818
So I still get to have it
in my life all the time,

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.053 size:81% position:41%
which is really great.
-That's really great.

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:28.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I'm certainly happy
to have it in mine.

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:29.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm so happy to have you here.
Thanks for being back.

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:31.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
Thanks for having me.

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:33.292 line:92%
-Always great to see you.

